1
00:00:00,399 --> 00:00:08,371
In 2022, only 61 percent of U.S. adults aged 45
to 75 were up to date on colon cancer screening.

2
00:00:10,791 --> 00:00:16,720
Parents often put their own checkups last. ScreenTalk
helps teens start the screening conversation at home.

3
00:00:17,093 --> 00:00:23,578
It follows American Cancer Society guidelines. It's education, not
diagnosis, and nothing you type leaves your device.

4
00:00:25,998 --> 00:00:31,244
Load a made-up demo family. Mom is 46,
so it's time to talk about breast,

5
00:00:31,264 --> 00:00:35,106
colon, and cervical cancer screening, each linked to the ACS guideline.

6
00:00:37,628 --> 00:00:42,155
Each topic also shows what the
U.S. Preventive Services Task Force says,

7
00:00:42,175 --> 00:00:47,459
tagged Same as ACS or Differs from
ACS, plus a note on no-copay coverage.

8
00:00:49,879 --> 00:00:56,167
Dad is 52 and quit smoking 18 years ago, so
his lung card explains where the two guidelines differ,

9
00:00:56,187 --> 00:00:58,823
and prostate testing is a choice to discuss.

10
00:01:00,294 --> 00:01:03,443
Adding someone takes seconds, and the pack-year helper does the math.

11
00:01:06,832 --> 00:01:10,446
Because Uncle still smokes, ScreenTalk links free help to quit.

12
00:01:15,769 --> 00:01:19,443
Each person also gets questions for the checkup, a progress tracker,

13
00:01:19,463 --> 00:01:20,786
and a calendar reminder.

14
00:01:23,251 --> 00:01:27,556
Now the hard part: bringing it up.
Tap Start the talk with Mom,

15
00:01:27,576 --> 00:01:31,215
and ScreenTalk writes an opener that names her exact topics. Casual,

16
00:01:31,235 --> 00:01:34,209
heartfelt, or a text. Edit it, then copy it.

17
00:01:36,735 --> 00:01:40,363
Parents push back, so you can
practice. Mom says, I feel fine.

18
00:01:40,383 --> 00:01:44,315
Pick a reply, and the coach explains
why it works, with a source.

19
00:01:49,755 --> 00:01:53,841
Lecture her about cost, and her openness drops.
At the end you get a score,

20
00:01:53,861 --> 00:01:56,579
Mom's final answer, and a better line for each round.

21
00:02:01,403 --> 00:02:03,726
One switch turns the whole app into Spanish.

22
00:02:06,146 --> 00:02:10,432
Load the demo family, and it's
Mamá, Papá, Abuela, and Hermana mayor.

23
00:02:14,647 --> 00:02:18,992
There's also a Myth or Fact
game sourced from NCI and ACS,

24
00:02:19,012 --> 00:02:21,175
plus free hotlines and screening programs.

25
00:02:22,231 --> 00:02:31,256
It's plain JavaScript, with no server and no tracking. 115 unit
tests and 246 browser checks keep every guideline boundary honest.

26
00:02:32,614 --> 00:02:37,419
ScreenTalk. You can't order your parents a
colonoscopy, but you can start the conversation.

